A suggestion for immutable variables like cardNumber or walletAddress can be made final like:
private final String cardNumber;

this means that the variable cannot be changed after initialization.

You can make variables like walletAddress or cardNumber be immutable on initialization and private using 
"private final"

private final String walletAddress;

Instead of using a and b, a good practice is to use parameter name for readability
so 
public SmartLight(int id, int brightness) {}

a and b can be 
public Thermostat(int id, double temperature) {}
for readability
